course: dictionary
lesson: 7066
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Patient» is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it and ask which meaning fits best.
explain: «In a hospital or doctor's waiting room you speak quietly and stay seated, because patients may be ill or worried.» Here patients are people being looked after by doctors. The clues are hospital, doctor and ill, so this is the noun meaning.
explain: Now read «a patient teacher». A teacher who explains a sum again and again without getting cross is calm and willing to wait. Here patient is an adjective that describes how someone behaves.
fact: Patient can be an adjective (describing a person) or a noun (a person).
fact: As an adjective, patient means able to wait calmly without getting cross or upset.
fact: Patient can also mean able to keep trying or explaining without giving up.
fact: As a noun, a patient is a person who is being looked after by a doctor, nurse or dentist.
fact: Useful phrases: «be patient», «patient with someone», «a hospital patient».
exercise: Mia waited in the queue for twenty minutes and did not complain once. Which word describes Mia? | Famous | Hungry | *Patient | Noisy
exercise: «It was reported that in many parts of England it became very hard to find an NHS dentist taking new patients.» What is a patient here? | *A person being looked after by a dentist | A person who is always calm | A tooth that hurts | A kind of dentist's chair
exercise: «Be patient, the bread is still baking.» What does patient mean here? | Hungry and in a hurry | A person being looked after by a doctor | *Able to wait calmly without getting cross | Very old
test: Sam kept trying the tricky puzzle and did not give up. Which meaning of patient fits? | *Able to keep trying without giving up | A person in hospital | Short and rude | Very old
test: «The doctor called the next patient into the room.» What is a patient in this sentence? | A room in a hospital | *A person being looked after by a doctor | Someone who is always cross | A calm and quiet teacher
exam: Dad waited calmly in the traffic jam without shouting. Which meaning of patient fits this sentence? | *Able to wait calmly without getting cross | Keeping on with a task that is hard and boring, and never giving up | Very old and wise | A person being looked after by a nurse
